{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Look down from Your holy abode, etc.</b> One needs to know why it repeated saying <b>מִמְּעוֹן</b> ('from the abode') and so on, <b>מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם</b> ('from the heavens'); and if it were to designate the name of His place, may He be blessed, in language of holiness, it should have said in this manner: ״הַשְׁקִיפָה מִמְּעוֹן וְגוֹ׳ הַשָּׁמַיִם״ ('Look down from Your abode, etc., the heavens')." "And it appears that the verse awakens one sod, namely that the Master, blessed be He, prepared two influxes above: one, the influx of spirituality — these being the pure souls; and one, the influx of good to sustain the created beings, which is food for all. And these two our Rabbis of blessed memory (Zohar ha-Kadosh) called זִוּוּג (pairing), for everything that has an aspect of bestower and an aspect of recipient can be called by the name זִוּוּג. And the mekubbalim said that from the day the Temple was destroyed the influx of souls was cut off, and there remained only the influx of the life of the worlds, which is compelled for the maintenance of the worlds. And this is what it says: <b>הַשְׁקִיפָה מִמְּעוֹן קָדְשְׁךָ</b> ('Look down from Your holy abode') — corresponding to the influx of souls; and this looking-down is supernal, in a high place called קֹדֶשׁ. And the mekubbalim have already revealed (Zohar vol. 2, 121a) the difference between the gradation of קֹדֶשׁ and the gradation of קָדוֹשׁ, for קָדוֹשׁ is higher — and the discerning one will understand. And corresponding to the influx of the life of the worlds it said ״מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם״ ('from the heavens'); this is a lower זִוּוּג than the first. And corresponding to the phrase ״הַשְׁקִיפָה״ it said ״וּבָרֵךְ אֶת עַמְּךָ״ ('and bless Your people'), which our Rabbis of blessed memory (Ma'aser Sheni 5:13) explained as with sons and daughters. And this validates our interpretation, that it speaks of the זִוּוּג of souls. And corresponding to the phrase ״מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם״ it said ״וְאֵת הָאֲדָמָה״ ('and the earth'), which is the blessing of food; and it is correct."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:08.390567369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}